Code review feedback identified overly complex regex for detecting existing age inferences in responses.

## Changes

- **Simplified detection logic in `#enforceAgeInference()`**: Replaced multi-pattern regex with explicit checks
  - `hasAgeInfo`: String search for "years old" or "age"
  - `hasSchoolLevel`: Pattern match for "kindergarten|preschool|first grade"
  - Combined with AND logic to skip inference when both present

## Before/After

**Before:**
```javascript
const ageInferencePattern = /\b([3-9]|1[0-8])\b.*?\b(years?\s+old|age)\b|kindergarten.*?\b([5-6]|five|six)\b/i;
if (ageInferencePattern.test(response)) {
  return { correctionApplied: false, response };
}
```

**After:**
```javascript
const hasAgeInfo = response.toLowerCase().includes('years old') || 
                   response.toLowerCase().includes('age');
const hasSchoolLevel = /kindergarten|preschool|first grade/i.test(response);

if (hasAgeInfo && hasSchoolLevel) {
  return { correctionApplied: false, response };
}
```

Maintains identical logic: validator skips enforcement when response already contains age context and school level mention.

